      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akiak%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Akiak sits on the west bank of the Kuskokwim River, 42 miles northeast of Bethel in the Yukon–Kuskokwim Delta.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akiak%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Akiak's post office was established in 1916, serving as a hub for communication.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akiak%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A public health hospital was built in the 1920s, providing essential care to the community.",
